index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..baebef69b0ec804669ec63a98786d5fd076ede9a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/ENGINEERING30_REPORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Engineering30 consumer intake and Shelf recovery
+
+Authorization: BRAIN-ONSKIN-AUTONOMOUS-LOCAL-PRODUCT-30. Starting source68dc086743f6c7f8b2ea8706aa973b27328b7814, tree613b11c549f4a46901c2ba819fb3db5a3d40ba61, branch stage/m1-native-runtime47. The initial worktree was clean and the active index was preserved before implementation. PR48's older source was not pulled or substituted.
+
+The unresolved daily-loop failure was reproduced at that exact clean source. Its driver touched the required opening choice below the viewport. The app correctly refused Add with no selected opening state. The repaired driver scrolls to the real control and verifies the reviewed choice; the original daily-loop assertions remain. The corrected375 browser diagnostic passed without changing application validation.
+
+Manual Cancel and opening Close now offer a contained keyboard-accessible decision: keep editing, explicitly save and leave, or leave without saving edits. Verified saves precede departure. Rejected or uncertain saves keep recovery available. Leaving clears working intake only; an existing saved revision is not discarded. Owner/consent/focus/session guards remain in every asynchronous completion. Opening choices now survive ordinary Back in the existing owner-bound memory context; reload still restores only explicit saved revisions.
+
+Saved-draft actions include product, position and revision in their accessible names, verification is announced, and discard owns keyboard focus with Escape/return. Each review has a new opaque identity. A canceled confirmation cannot be revived by reopening the same saved row. Concurrent revision refusal retires the dialog and exposes the actual refresh recovery. Captured background category/save/Add controls cannot act through the leave decision.
+
+Opening review distinguishes raw barcode/text from normalized barcode and parsed ingredient entries, explains parser uncertainty, and explicitly distinguishes a Shelf admission from actual routine application or use. No label, product, clinical or provider authority is created by parsing. Existing encryption, source reservation, CAS, stable attempted Add identity, canonical readback and exact draft retirement remain unchanged.
+
+The connected local browser campaign follows explicit adult/consent onboarding, encrypted incomplete draft/reload/resume, opening review/Add, actual saved product readback, separate explicit bottle observation/correction, free routine review/cancel/apply, a separate visible keyboard check-off bound to the exact product/formula/version, reload and Shelf removal without intake resurrection. It also exercises multiple unnamed drafts, failed save-and-leave, acknowledged-loss recovery by exact saved-revision inspection, concurrent discard conflict and narrow/large-text behavior. Invented owner/product/transcription inputs and deliberate storage/acknowledgement faults are labelled synthetic.
+
+RED/GREEN traces cover unconfirmed cancellation, stale discard-review revival, competing category activation and conflict recovery. All original source/authority/storage assertions remain. The existing bottle-resume test now waits for the actual enabled current-source control after remount, matching its initial-entry readiness check; its disabled/identity/content assertions are retained. A professional finite-history test exceeded its unchanged timeout during concurrent broad checks; the failed run is retained and final uncached validation is run with workspace tasks serialized.
+
